      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, `ffi::native_handle_t` is the type generated by bindgen from the C `native_handle_t` struct. The C header is the canonical documentation for its layout so I\u0027d rather not duplicate that in a comment here where it might get out of date.\n\nIf `RawFd` is not the same type as `c_int` then this will fail to compile, which I think is what we want because it suggests something is wrong.\n\n`slice::from_raw_parts_mut` requires that the data is initialised, which it is not at this point, so that would be unsound. `native_handle_create` allocates enough space for both the header and the data, but only initialises the header. We are responsible for initialising the data, which is what this code is doing. Added a comment saying that.",
